{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"code":["        \/\/ Assuming in Figma with have a elevation semantic token none,","        \/\/ with values depending to color scheme. These values are defined as elevation raw tokens.","        let bottom_0 = ElevationCompositeRawToken(x: x0, y: y0, blur: blur0, color: ColorRawTokens.opacityBlack0)","        let bottom_1_100 = ElevationCompositeRawToken(x: x0, y: y100, blur: blur200, color: ColorRawTokens.opacityBlack100)","","        \/\/ Then the develoment team declares an \"higher\" level elevation semantic token","        \/\/ inside ElevationCompositeSemanticTokens protocol,","        \/\/ and defined inside BlueCoatTheme+ElevationCompositeSemanticTokens extension","        \/\/ ElevationCompositeSemanticToken is a typealias for MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken to keep same grammar as design kit","        var none: ElevationCompositeSemanticToken {","            ElevationCompositeSemanticToken(light: bottom_0, dark: bottom_1_100)","        }","","        \/\/ If the same elevation is used whatever the color scheme is","        var none: ElevationCompositeSemanticToken {","            ElevationCompositeSemanticToken(bottom_0)","        }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"code":["        \/\/ The theme exposes both generated elevation semantic tokens and \"crafted\" higher level elevation semantic tokens.","        \/\/ It is recommended to use the higher level version as it is less error-prone.","","        @Environment(\\.theme) var theme","        @Environment(\\.colorScheme) var colorScheme","","        \/\/ Given you want to apply the elevation token \"raised\"","        var body: some View {","            \/\/ Apply the token of elevation for the shadow effect without managing yourself the color scheme","            Rectangle()","                .shadow(elevation: theme.elevations.raised))","        }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"code":["    \/\/ Or get the token depending to the color scheme and do whatever you want with","    theme.elevations.raised.elevation(for: colorScheme)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The case of this ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"},{"type":"text","text":" is quite particular because in fact it contains "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"},{"type":"text","text":" (i.e. raw tokens) instead of semantic tokens."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In fact only the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"color"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" of the elevation effect vary depending to the color scheme,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figma"}]},{"text":" kit this is composite raw tokens which are defined for ligh and dark mode as only one token.","type":"text"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS 0.8.0"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Since"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Semantic tokens which will wrap a combination of ","type":"text"},{"code":"ElevationCompositeRawToken","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" depending to color scheme (i.e. light mode or dark mode)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Kind of composite token with multiple values, but not named “composite” because this word is already used in the design system.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Allows to gather the multiple-value tokens from "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"text","text":" inside one object."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If an elevation token exists with its value depending to the color scheme, it must be packed in such ``MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken`"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","symbolKind":"class","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Tokens for semantics"}],"platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"15.0"},{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"13.0"},{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"1.0"},{"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"11.0"}],"externalID":"c:@M@MISOTokensSemantic@objc(cs)MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"}],"title":"MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/misotokenssemantic\/multipleelevationcompositerawtoken"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationCompositeRawToken\/init(light:dark:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleElevationComposit